+section('quick-start', 'Quick start', 'rocket-takeoff')
  p Five steps from nothing to a first job. Every step links to its full section.
  ol.thub-help-steps
    li
      strong Install the Coordinator
      |  on a cloud VM behind an HTTPS reverse proxy (#[a(href="#coordinator") Coordinator setup]):
      +code('Coordinator host').
        sudo npm i -g @andrian.yablonskyy/thub-coordinator
        thub-admin join-key generate          # → put it in clientJoinKey
        nano ~/.config/thub/coordinator.json  # publicUrl, clientJoinKey
        sudo systemctl restart thub-coordinator
        thub-admin create-admin admin 'a-strong-password'
    li
      strong Install a Client
      |  on each lab machine, with the same join key (#[a(href="#client-setup") Client setup]):
      +code('Lab machine (Ubuntu 26.04)').
        sudo apt install -y nodejs npm docker.io      # + stlink-tools openocd for HW
        sudo npm i -g @andrian.yablonskyy/thub-client
        nano ~/.config/thub/client.json               # coordinatorUrl, type, joinKey
        sudo systemctl enable --now thub-client@client
      | It shows up on #[a(href="/resources") Resources] by itself, usually within 10 s.
    li
      strong Issue an agent token
      |  on #[a(href="/admin/agents") Agents] (admins), or on the Coordinator host with
      |  #[code thub-admin agent add &lt;name&gt; --kind ci|cli]. The token is shown once.
    li
      strong Install and configure the Agent
      |  (#[a(href="#agent-setup") Agent setup]):
      +code('Developer machine').
        npm i -g @andrian.yablonskyy/thub-agent
        thub config set url #{coordinatorUrl}
        thub config set token agt_…
    li
      strong Run a job
      |  (#[a(href="#agent-cli") Agent CLI reference]):
      +code('Developer machine').
        thub run --type sw --command 'uname -a && echo hello from the lab' --wait
